    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nWith cython 3.3.0, pyx files fails to compile if using the Python `str` type in a comparison with a bytestring. Similar code works for the longest time since 0.29.XX days. Can confirm it compiles if cythonized with cython 3.2.9.\n\n\nChuggs with the following error, which makes me think the new comparison code introduced in cython 3.3.0 is not treating byte strings correctly. This only addresses the compilation error. Not sure if the comparison is even valid after the compilation because I can't test it.\n```\n  File \"/Users/User/miniconda3/envs/westpa-2022.15/lib/python3.13/site-packages/Cython/Compiler/ExprNodes.py\", line 14444, in find_special_bool_compare_function\n    character = ord(self.operand2.value[0])\nTypeError: ord() expected string of length 1, but int found\n```\n\n<details>\n<summary>full error message </summary>\n\n```\n(westpa-2022.15) MacBookPro:westpa-2022.15 User$ cythonize _test.pyx\nCompiling /Users/User/Documents/Important/Pitt/git/westpa-2022.15/_test.pyx because it changed.\n[1/1] Cythonizing /Users/User/Documents/Important/Pitt/git/westpa-2022.15/_test.pyx\n\nError compiling Cython file:\n------------------------------------------------------------\n...\ncdef:\n    str _a\n\n_a = 'a'\n\nif _a == b'a':\n      ^\n------------------------------------------------------------\n_test.pyx:6:6: Compiler crash in AnalyseExpressionsTransform\n\nFile 'Nodes.py', line 430, in analyse_expressions: StatListNode(_test.pyx:1:0)\nFile 'Nodes.py', line 7423, in analyse_expressions: IfStatNode(_test.pyx:6:0)\nFile 'Nodes.py', line 7469, in analyse_expressions: IfClauseNode(_test.pyx:6:3)\nFile 'ExprNodes.py', line 720, in analyse_temp_boolean_expression: PrimaryCmpNode(_test.pyx:6:6,\n    operator = '==',\n    result_is_used = True,\n    use_managed_ref = True)\nFile 'ExprNodes.py', line 14711, in analyse_types: PrimaryCmpNode(_test.pyx:6:6,\n    operator = '==',\n    result_is_used = True,\n    use_managed_ref = True)\nFile 'ExprNodes.py', line 14444, in find_special_bool_compare_function: PrimaryCmpNode(_test.pyx:6:6,\n    operator = '==',\n    result_is_used = True,\n    use_managed_ref = True)\n\nCompiler crash traceback from this point on:\n  File \"/Users/User/miniconda3/envs/westpa-2022.15/lib/python3.13/site-packages/Cython/Compiler/ExprNodes.py\", line 14444, in find_special_bool_compare_function\n    character = ord(self.operand2.value[0])\nTypeError: ord() expected string of length 1, but int found\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/Users/User/miniconda3/envs/westpa-2022.15/bin/cythonize\", line 11, in <module>\n    sys.exit(main())\n             ~~~~^^\n  File \"/Users/User/miniconda3/envs/westpa-2022.15/lib/python3.13/site-packages/Cython/Build/Cythonize.py\", line 324, in main\n    ext_modules_by_basedir = _cython_compile_files(all_paths, options)\n  File \"/Users/User/miniconda3/envs/westpa-2022.15/lib/python3.13/site-packages/Cython/Build/Cythonize.py\", line 51, in _cython_compile_files\n    ext_modules = cythonize(\n        paths,\n    ...<8 lines>...\n        language=options.language,\n        **options.options)\n  File \"/Users/User/miniconda3/envs/westpa-2022.15/lib/python3.13/site-packages/Cython/Build/Dependencies.py\", line 1153, in cythonize\n    cythonize_one(*args)\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^\n  File \"/Users/User/miniconda3/envs/westpa-2022.15/lib/python3.13/site-packages/Cython/Build/Dependencies.py\", line 1264, in cythonize_one\n    raise CompileError(None, pyx_file)\nCython.Compiler.Errors.CompileError: /Users/User/Documents/Important/Pitt/git/westpa-2022.15/_test.pyx\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\nin _test.pyx:\n```cython\ncdef:\n     str _a\n\n_a = 'a' \n\nif _a == b'a':\n    pass\n```\n\nRun:\n```\ncythonize _test.pyx\n```\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nCythonization without fail, like in cython <=3.2.9\n\nNote that if the comparison is with `'a'` and not `b'a'`, it compiles fine. Same with setting `_a` to `bytes` or `int`\n\n\n\n### OS\n\nLinux, MacOS\n\n### Python version\n\n3.10 ~ 3.14\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3.0\n\n### Additional context\n\nhttps://github.com/westpa/westpa/actions/runs/32744608514/job/97487263287\n\nAll our (`westpa`'s) latest builds are failing with the same error so... I'm pretty sure it's universal.\n\nEDIT: Updated with a more concise example.",
