        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> it should just compile to `if False:`\n\nIt _should_, but it's not easy to do. Constant folding doesn't handle it because the LHS isn't a constant, so we would have to add special cases based on known types (in addition to known values) – _if_ we know the type. But adding a bunch of code for something that is very uncommon in real code seems not worth it.\n\nIt's easy to fix the bug, though. The optimised str-character comparison code was just too eager to take over, even when comparing str to a bytes literal. It should only apply to str literals.",
